{"id": "EUVD-2026-74264", "enisaUuid": "af4c598d-c19e-337f-90e6-ce2eb61e4822", "description": "A memory corruption vulnerability exists in FFmpeg before 8.1. The RTP encoding process. In the nal_send function in libavformat/rtpenc_h264_hevc.c, a negative size parameter (size=-3) is passed to memcpy when transmitting H.264/HEVC streams via RTP using a crafted input file. This was detected using AddressSanitizer.", "datePublished": "2026-09-08T00:00:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-09T15:18:09", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/20746", "https://github.com/momo-trip/poc_ffmpeg", "https://gist.github.com/momo-trip/4cddf2c9e15600873de55259dac6b0e6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-30754", "GHSA-crqp-42h3-7fcv"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6f99f06e-d4fb-34aa-983d-8bc21b2e6cb2", "product": {"name": "n/a", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "n/a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "912da5dc-f6a4-331b-b71f-6915fb1a9e74", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}], "isExploited": false}